<http://data.silknow.org/object/d96e4311-fd1e-37cc-a376-e6c1e561c78d>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Man's court coat, 1785-90, French/English; Figured brown ribbed silk, embroidered, altered 1870-1910"@en , "A man’s court coat of figured brown ribbed silk, with a 3¼ -inch (8.3 cm) standing collar, 2-piece sleeves ending in cuffs 4¼  inches (10.7 cm) deep.  The fronts curve from neck to hem with pleats 2¾ inches (7 cm) deep, below the hip set beside the centre back.  Each front has a pocket and shaped pocket flap; the centre-back seam is open below the hip.   The coat, sleeves and pocket flaps are lined with cream silk satin, the pockets with bleached linen.  The coat is embroidered-to-shape with silk floss in shades of green, blue, lilac and white in a pattern of lilac and trump-shaped flowers, on the collar, cuffs and pocket flaps, around the pockets, along the fronts and centre-back opening.  There were 8 embroidered buttons along the right front and 2 on each cuff.  \n\nThe coat was probably worn as theatre costume in the late 19th century.  The lining was patched and repaired, the pleats have been rearranged and buttons moved and resewn. The spangles once at the centre of the embroidered flowers were removed. The two buttonholes on the left front were added."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/23a6bb85-68cd-3404-b345-55f342d0686e> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/5984bc77-8f7a-374f-ba0f-977dacaa0f80> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/ebe8374b-12fd-359b-afae-053cb2cfba3e> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/69fec5f4-2c37-3e6d-9055-85e2bd5b25c9> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/8f36add1-11a7-3cd4-abce-4e841dd4e8fb> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/e166f8e0-9213-32b5-bb52-2e5cdd1c2ef9> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/fe200e53-c62f-3dbe-8af1-70f6bf2df35b> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Man's court coat, 1785-90, French/English; Figured brown ribbed silk, embroidered, altered 1870-1910"@en , "A man’s court coat of figured brown ribbed silk, with a 3¼ -inch (8.3 cm) standing collar, 2-piece sleeves ending in cuffs 4¼  inches (10.7 cm) deep.  The fronts curve from neck to hem with pleats 2¾ inches (7 cm) deep, below the hip set beside the centre back.  Each front has a pocket and shaped pocket flap; the centre-back seam is open below the hip.   The coat, sleeves and pocket flaps are lined with cream silk satin, the pockets with bleached linen.  The coat is embroidered-to-shape with silk floss in shades of green, blue, lilac and white in a pattern of lilac and trump-shaped flowers, on the collar, cuffs and pocket flaps, around the pockets, along the fronts and centre-back opening.  There were 8 embroidered buttons along the right front and 2 on each cuff.  \n\nThe coat was probably worn as theatre costume in the late 19th century.  The lining was patched and repaired, the pleats have been rearranged and buttons moved and resewn. The spangles once at the centre of the embroidered flowers were removed. The two buttonholes on the left front were added."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/d96e4311-fd1e-37cc-a376-e6c1e561c78d/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/d96e4311-fd1e-37cc-a376-e6c1e561c78d/dimension/2> ;
